      {
        "kind": "text",
        "heading": "The rules of differentiation",
        "body": {
          "en": "We rarely use the limit definition directly. These rules build every elementary derivative:",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}x^{n}=n\\,x^{\\,n-1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Constant multiple",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\big(c\\,f\\big)=c\\,f' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (f+g)'=f'+g' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( (fg)'=f'g+fg' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\Big(\\dfrac{f}{g}\\Big)'=\\dfrac{f'g-fg'}{g^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Chain",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}f\\big(g(x)\\big)=f'\\!\\big(g(x)\\big)\\,g'(x) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Common derivatives",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sin x=\\cos x \\), \\(\\quad \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\cos x=-\\sin x \\), \\(\\quad \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\tan x=\\sec^2 x \\),</p><p>\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}e^{x}=e^{x} \\), \\(\\quad \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\ln x=\\dfrac1x \\quad (x&gt;0). \\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.A — Chain rule",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( y=\\sin\\!\\big(3x^2\\big) \\).</p><p>Outer function \\( \\sin u \\) with \\( u=3x^2 \\). Then \\( \\dfrac{dy}{du}=\\cos u \\) and \\( \\dfrac{du}{dx}=6x \\). By the chain rule,</p>\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\cos\\!\\big(3x^2\\big)\\cdot 6x = 6x\\cos\\!\\big(3x^2\\big). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 2.B — Product rule",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( y=x^2 e^{x} \\).</p><p>With \\( f=x^2 \\) (so \\( f'=2x \\)) and \\( g=e^x \\) (so \\( g'=e^x \\)):</p>\\[ y'=2x\\,e^{x}+x^2 e^{x}=x e^{x}(x+2). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
